  "text": "proprium.beatae-mariae-virginis-a-rosario-epistola",
  "about": "The epistola of the formulary “Blessed Virgin Mary of the Rosary” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": {
      "translation": "The Lord begot me, the firstborn of His ways, the forerunner of His prodigies of long ago; from of old I was poured forth, at the first, before the earth. When there were no depths I was brought forth. So now, O children, listen to me; happy those who keep my ways. Hear instruction, and be wise, and refuse it not. Happy the man who obeys me, watching daily at my gates, waiting at my doorposts; for he who finds me finds life, and wins favor from the Lord."
    }
  },
